. Adding those gives 6300 + 540 = 6840. Then multiply by 10 to get 68,400. Wait, no, that's incorrect. Wait, actually, 760 × 90 is 760 × 9 × 10, so 760 × 9 is 6840, then times 10 is 68,400. Yes, that's right. So second step is 68,400.\n\nThird step is the hundreds place. The hundreds digit in 998 is 9, which represents 900. So multiplying 760 by 900. Let's see. 760 × 900 can be broken down as 760 × 9 × 100. First, 760 × 9 again is 6,840, then multiplied by 100 gives 684,000. .\n\nNow, I need to sum all three results: 6,080 (from ones) + 68,400 (from tens) + 684,000 (from hundreds). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 6,080 + 68,400. Adding those together: 6,080 + 68,400 = 74,480. Then add that to 684,000. So 74,480 + 684,000. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
