final_output:  ['\n\nTo find the product of 968 and 729, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 968 by the ones place digit (9) of 729:**\n   \\[\n   968 \\times 9 = 8712\n   \\]\n   - \\(900 \\times 9 = 8100\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 9 = 540\\)\n   - \\(8 \\times 9 = 72\\)\n   - Summing these: \\(8100 + 540 + 72 = 8712\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 968 by the tens place digit (20) of 729:**\n   \\[\n   968 \\times 20 = 19360\n   \\]\n   - \\(968 \\times 2 = 1936\\)\n   - Adding a zero: \\(1936 \\times 10 = 19360\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 968 by the hundreds place digit (700) of 729:**\n   \\[\n   968 \\times 700 = 677600\n   \\]\n   - \\(968 \\times 7 = 6776\\)\n   - Adding two zeros: \\(6776 \\times 100 = 677600\\)\n\n**Summing all the results:**\n\\[\n8712 + 19360 + 677600 = 705672\n\\]\n- First, add \\(8712 + 19360\\):\n  \\[\n  8712 + 19360 = 28072\n  \\]\n- Then add the result to \\(677600\\):\n  \\[\n  28072 + 677600 = 705672\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{705672}\\).', '677,600 + 28,072 = 705,672. Wait, but the user initially thought the answer was 705,674? Hmm, so there must be an error in my calculation somewhere.\n\nWait, let me check all steps again carefully.\n\nFirst step: 968 × 9 (ones place):\n\n900×9=8100, 60×9=540, 8×9=72. Adding those: 8100+540 is 8640, plus 72 gives 8712. That\'s correct.\n\nSecond step: 968 × 20 (tens place):\n\n968 ×2 = 1936, then ×10 gives 19,360. Correct.\n\nThird step: 968 ×700 (hundreds place):\n\n968 ×7 = 6,776. Then ×100 gives 677,600. That\'s correct.\n\nNow adding the three results:\n\nFirst sum: 8,712 +19,360 = 28,072 (as before).\n\n28,072 + 677,600. Let\'s add 28,072 + 600,000 = 628,072. Then add 77,600 more: 628,072 +70,000 = 698,072, then +7,600 = 705,672. So total is 705,672.\n\nBut the user\'s initial thought was 705,674. So there\'s a discrepancy of 2. That means I must have made a mistake somewhere.\n\nLet me recheck all steps again.\n\nStarting with the first multiplication: 968 ×9.\n\n9×900: 8100. 9×60: 540. 9×8:72. Adding those: 8100 +540 is 8640. 8640+72=8712. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 968×20. 968×2=1936. 1936×10=19,360. Correct.\n\nThird step: 968×700. Let\'s recompute 968×7. Let\'s do it digit by digit:\n\n900×7=6300. 60×7=420. 8×7=56. 6300+420=6720. 6720+56=6776. So 6776×100=677,600. That\'s correct.\n\nAdding all three: 8,712 +19,360 = 28,072. Then 28,072 +677,600 = 705,672. Hmm, so the correct answer should be 705,672, but the user thought it was 705,674. Therefore, the user\'s initial answer is off by 2. So my calculation seems correct. Maybe the user made a mistake?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made an error in one of the steps. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe when adding 8,712 +19,360. Let me do that again:\n\n8,712\n\n+19,360\n\n= ?\n\nAdding units:\n\n2 +0 =2\n\n1 +6 =7\n\n7 +3 =10 (so 0 with carryover 1)\n\n8 +9 =17, plus the 1 carried over is 18. So the thousands place is 8 and carryover 1 to the next digit (ten thousands place). The ten thousands place is 1 (from the 19,360\'s 1 in the ten thousands place?), Wait, actually, let me write it out properly:\n\n\u2003\u20038,712\n\n+19,360\n\n------------\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n\u2003\u2003\xa08,712\n\n+19,360\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 +0 =2\n\nTens:1 +6 =7\n\nHundreds:7 +3 =10 → 0 with carryover 1\n\nThousands:8 +9 =17, plus 1 carried over is 18 → 8 in thousands place, carryover 1 to ten-thousands.\n\nTen-thousands place: 1 (from the 19,360\'s 1) plus the carried over 1 → 2.\n\nSo the total is 28,072. That\'s correct.\n\nThen adding 28,072 +677,600:\n\n28,072 +677,600:\n\n28,072 + 600,000 = 628,072\n\n628,072 +77,600 = ?\n\n628,072 +70,000 = 698,072\n\n698,072 +7,600 = 705,672. Correct.\n\nHmm, so the correct answer is 705,672. The user\'s answer was 705,674. Therefore, the user is off by 2. Maybe they made a mistake in their calculation. Let me see where that discrepancy could come from.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in multiplying