final_output:  ['', '172,500 + 4,718 = 177,218? Wait, wait, no, hold on. Wait, I think I made a miscalculation here. Wait, 168500 plus 4718. Let\'s do this properly:\n\n168500\n\n+\xa0 4718\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +8 =8\n\n0 +1 =1\n\n5 +7 =12, carryover 1.\n\n8 +4 +1 (carryover) =13, carryover 1.\n\n6 +1 (carryover) =7.\n\n1 remains.\n\nSo:\n\n168500\n\n+\xa0 4718\n\n= 173,218? Let me check:\n\n168,500 + 4,000 is 172,500. Then 172,500 + 718 = 173,218. Yes, that\'s correct. But wait, the user\'s initial answer was 173,248. Hmm, so that suggests that I might have made an error here. Let me retrace my steps.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the partial products? Let me check each step again.\n\nFirst partial product: 337 ×4 =1348. That seems right.\n\nSecond partial product: 337 ×1 (tens place digit), so shifted once: 3370. That\'s correct.\n\nThird partial product: 337 ×5 (hundreds place digit, so 500), so 337×5=1685, shifted two places: 168500. That\'s correct.\n\nAdding them: 1348 +3370 =4718. Then 4718 +168500. Let\'s do 168,500 +4,718:\n\n168,500 + 4,718:\n\nAdding 168,500 +4,000 =172,500\n\n172,500 +718 =173,218.\n\nHmm, so according to my calculation, the total is 173,218, but the user\'s answer is 173,248. There\'s a discrepancy here. So where did I go wrong?\n\nWait a second, perhaps I made an error in multiplying one of the steps. Let me check each partial product again.\n\nFirst step: 337 ×4.\n\n337 ×4:\n\n7×4=28, carryover 2.\n\n3×4=12 +2=14, write 4, carryover1.\n\n3×4=12 +1=13. So 1348. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 337 ×1 (tens place). So 337 ×10 =3370. Correct.\n\nThird step: 337 ×5 (hundreds place digit, so 500). 337 ×5:\n\nLet me recalculate 337×5 again.\n\n300×5=1500\n\n30×5=150 → total so far 1650\n\n7×5=35 → total 1685. So that\'s correct. Then 1685 ×100 =168,500. Correct.\n\nHmm, so the partial products are correct. Then adding them again: 1348 +3370 =4718. Then 4718 +168500.\n\nWait 168500 +4718:\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n168500\n\