should be shifted one position to the left. .\n\nFirst, compute 758 ×4. Let's see:.\n\n4 ×8 =32. Write down 2, carryover 3.\n\n4×5=20 +3=23. Write 3, carryover 2.\n\n4×7=28 +2=30. So that gives 3032. Then, since it's the tens place, multiply by 10, so 30320.\n\nWait, actually, 758 ×40 is the same as 758 ×4 ×10, so 3032 ×10 =30320. That seems right.\n\nNow the hundreds place of 447 is the first digit, which is 4 (but it's 400). So multiply 758 by 400. .\n\nAgain, 758 ×4 is 3032, so times 100 would be 303200. .\n\nNow I need to add all three results together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 5306.\n\nSecond partial product: 30320.\n\nThird partial product: 303200.\n\nAdding them up step by step. Let me line them up properly:.\n\n      5306.\n    +30320.\n    -------.\n     35626 (5306 +30320 = 35626?).\n\nWait, 5306 +30320. Let me compute that again. 5306 + 30,000 is 35306, then add 320: 35306 +320 =35626. Yes.\n\nThen add the third partial product: 35626 +303200. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
