computed product is \\boxed{684019}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 703 and 973?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 973 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps:\n\n1. Multiply 703 by the ones place digit 3 of 973:\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 3 = 2109\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 703 by the tens place digit 70 of 973:\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 70 = 703 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 4921 \\times 10 = 49210\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 703 by the hundreds place digit 900 of 973:\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 900 = 703 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 6327 \\times 100 = 632700\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n2109 + 49210 + 632700 = 684019\n\\]\n\nAnswer: The final computed product is \\boxed{684019}.",
