ace, so 7\u00d7571=3997, then shift one position to the left: 39970).\n\nThen multiply by 200 (hundreds place, 2\u00d7571=1142, shift two positions: 114200).\n\nAdding them up: 2855 + 39970 = 42,825; then 42,825 + 114,200 = 157,025. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 571 \u00d7275 using another method. Let's see:\n\n571 \u00d7 275 = 571 \u00d7 (200 + 70 +5) = 571\u00d7200 +571\u00d770 +571\u00d75 = same as before.\n\nAlternatively, use a calculator? Well, since I can't use a calculator, maybe do 571 \u00d7275:\n\nLet me compute 571 \u00d7275 step by step differently.\n\nAlternatively, 571 \u00d7275 = 571 \u00d7 (25 \u00d711) since 275 =25\u00d711. Hmm, not sure if that helps.\n\nAlternatively, 275 \u00d7571:\n\nLet me try the multiplication vertically:\n\n       571\n     \u00d7 275\n     --------\n        2855  (571\u00d75)\n       3997   (571\u00d77, shifted one position)\n      1142    (571\u00d72, shifted two positions)\n     ---------\n      ?\n\nWait, but when shifted two positions, it's actually 114200, so:\n\nAdding:\n\n       2855\n      39970\n    +114200\n    ---------\n    Let's align them:\n\n          2855\n         39970\n        114200\n    -----------\n    Adding the thousands:\n\n    2855\n    +39970 = 42825\n\n    42825 +114200:\n\n    42,825 + 114,200 = 157,025. So yes, same result.\n\nHmm, so the correct answer should be 157,025, but the user says they think it's 157,021. So perhaps the user made an error in their calculation steps.\n\nWait, maybe I miscalculated one of the components. Let me check 571 \u00d75 again: 5\u00d7500=2500, 5\u00d770=350, 5\u00d71=5. 2500+350 is 2850, plus 5 is 2855. Correct.\n\n571\u00d77: 7\u00d7500=3500, 7\u00d770=490, 7\u00d71=7. 3500+490=3990 +7=3997. Then \u00d710 gives 39,970. Correct.\n\n571\u00d72=1142, \u00d7100 is 114,200. Correct.\n\nAdding all three: 2855+39970=42,825. 42,825 +114,200. Let's see:\n\n42,825 + 114,200:\n\n42,825 + 100,000 = 142,825.\n\n142,825 +14,200 = 157,025. Correct.\