=120, 2*6=12. 1800+120 is 1920, plus 12 is 1932. So yes, times 100 is 193,200.\n\nNow, I need to add all three results together: 966 (from the ones) + 25,760 (from the tens) + 193,200 (from the hundreds). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 966 + 25,760. Let's see: 25,760 + 900 is 26,660, then plus 66 more is 26,726. Wait, maybe another way: 25,760 + 966. 25,760 + 900 = 26,660, then +66 = 26,726. .\n\nThen add that to 193,200. So 26,726 + 193,200. Let's add 193,200 + 26,726. 193,200 + 20,000 is 213,200. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
