git, 3\u00d7100): 292\u00d7300 =87,600\n\nThen sum them: 1,460 +11,680 =13,140; then 13,140 +87,600 =100,740.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 100,740, not 100,780. \n\nSo, in the template, the user might have made an error in the addition step. \n\nFollowing the structure:\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 345 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 292 by the ones place digit 5 of 345: 292 \u00d75 = 1,460\n2. Multiply 292 by the tens place digit 40 of 345: 292 \u00d740 = 11,680\n3. Multiply 292 by the hundreds place digit 300 of 345: 292 \u00d7300 =87,600\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 1,460 + 11,680 +87,600 =100,740.\nSo, the final computed product is 100,740.\n\nTherefore, the user's initial thought was incorrect, and the correct answer is 100,740. \n\nI should present this in the required template format, replacing the placeholders with the correct numbers and steps as above.\n</think>\n\n",
