dred thousands: 1 (from 180,200) + carried 1 =2.\n\nSo putting it all together: 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 4 (hundreds?), wait wait, let's see:\n\nWait the breakdown:\n\nHundred thousands place: 1 (from 180,200) plus carryover from ten thousands. Wait let's do it step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:8\n\nTens:3\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands place: 4 (from 34,238) +0 (from 180,200) =4\n\nTen thousands place:3 (from 34,238) +8 (from 180,200) =11. So we write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands place: 1 (from 180,200) plus the carried over 1 =2.\n\nSo the total is 214,438. \n\nHmm, so the correct answer is 214,438, but the user thought it was 214,430. So perhaps they made a mistake in their calculation. Let me check where they might have gone wrong. Maybe in the addition steps.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made an error in one of the multiplications. Let me recheck each multiplication.\n\nFirst multiplication: 901 \u00d78. 900\u00d78=7200, plus 1\u00d78=8 \u2192 7208. Correct.\n\nSecond: 901 \u00d730. Since it's the tens place, the 3 is in tens place so 30. 901 \u00d730. Let me compute 901\u00d73=2703, then \u00d710 gives 27,030. Correct.\n\nThird: 901 \u00d7200. 901\u00d72=1802, so \u00d7100 is 180,200. Correct.\n\nAdding all three: 7,208 +27,030 =34,238. Then adding 180,200: 34,238 +180,200 =214,438. So that's correct. The user's answer is 214,430. The difference is 214,438 vs 214,430, so they might have subtracted 8 somewhere? Maybe in the first step they thought 901\u00d78 was 7200 +8=7208, but maybe they miscalculated 900\u00d78 as 7200, but 1\u00d78=8, so that's correct. Alternatively, maybe they thought the second multiplication was 901\u00d750 (but no, the tens digit is 3). Wait, the number is 238, so digits are 2 (hundreds), 3 (tens),8 (ones). So all steps are correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the user made an error in adding. Let me check their supposed answer of 214,430. Let's see what would happen