o digits gives 141600. Correct.\n\nAdding all three: 2478 +28320 = 30,798. Then 30,798 +141,600 = 172,398. Yes, that\'s correct. So the user\'s answer of 772,398 is wrong. Maybe they thought the first number was 3540 or something. Let me check 3540 × 487:\n\n3540 ×487. Let\'s see, 3540 × 487 is 354×10 ×487 =354×4870. That would be way larger. 354×4870 is 354×487×10, so 1,723,980. Not 772,398.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they multiplied 354 × 2,182? Let me see 2,182 × 354. Let\'s compute that:\n\n2,182 × 300 = 654,600.\n\n2,182 ×50 = 109,100.\n\n2,182 ×4 = 8,728.\n\nAdding those: 654,600 +109,100 =763,700. Then +8,728 is 772,428. Close to their 772,398 but not exactly. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they had a typo in the numbers. Maybe the question was 354 × 2,182 but written as 354×487. Not sure. Alternatively, maybe I miscalculated. Wait, let me do 354 ×487 using another method.\n\nLet me do 354 ×487 as (350 +4) × (400 +80 +7).\n\nFirst, 350×400 =140,000.\n\n350×80 =28,000.\n\n350×7 =2,450.\n\nThen 4×400 =1,600.\n\n4×80 =320.\n\n4×7 =28.\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n140,000 +28,000 =168,000.\n\n168,000 +2,450 =170,450.\n\n170,450 +1,600 =172,050.\n\n172,050 +320 =172,370.\n\n172,370 +28 =172,398. Same result again.\n\nTherefore, I\'m confident the correct answer is 172,398. The user\'s answer of 772,398 is incorrect. Perhaps they made a mistake in the multiplication steps, maybe adding an extra digit somewhere, or miscalculating one of the partial products.\n\nWait, let me check the user\'s answer. 772,398. If I divide that by 354, what do I get? 772,398 ÷354 ≈ 2,182. So that would mean the second number should be 2,182 instead of 487. So maybe they multiplied 354×2182. Alternatively, perhaps the original problem had different numbers, but the user mistyped. Alternatively, maybe they thought 487 was 2,182. Not sure. But according to the problem given, 354×487 is 172,398.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 172,398, and the user\'s proposed answer is incorrect. I\'l