lts:\n\nFirst result: 178\n\nSecond result: 3,560\n\nThird result: 106,800\n\nAdding them together:\n\n178 + 3,560 = 3,738\n\nThen 3,738 + 106,800 = 110,538.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 110,538. The user's answer of 130,538 is incorrect, likely due to an addition error where perhaps they added 106,800 + 35,600 (mistaking 3,560 as 35,600), which would give 142,400, but that doesn't align. Alternatively, maybe they miscalculated the hundreds place. But regardless, following the correct steps, the answer is 110,538.\n\nSo I'll present this in the template provided.\n</think>\n\n",
