at confirms it again. So the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{501030}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 879 and 570, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 570 (500, 70, and 0):\n\n1. **Multiply 879 by 500:**\n   \\[\n   879 \\times 500 = 879 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 4395 \\times 100 = 439500\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 879 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   879 \\times 70 = 879 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 6153 \\times 10 = 61530\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 879 by 0:**\n   \\[\n   879 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n439500 + 61530 + 0 = 501030\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{501030}\\).",
