e verify. 940 * 700. 940*7 is 6,580. Then times 100 gives 658,000. That's correct.\n\nAdding them:\n\n7,520 +28,200 = 35,720. Then 35,720 +658,000 = 693,720. \n\nHmm, so the correct answer should be 693,720, but the user's initial thought was 613,720. So maybe the user made an error in their calculation. Let me see where they might have gone wrong.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in the partial products. Let me check again.\n\nWait, perhaps when multiplying 940 by 700, I considered 700 as part of 738, but actually, the hundreds digit is 7, so 7*100, so yes, 700. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe when adding the partial products, there was an error. Let me re-add all three numbers:\n\nFirst partial product: 7,520\n\nSecond partial product: 28,200\n\nThird partial product: 658,000\n\nTotal: 7,520 +28,200 = 35,720. Then 35,720 +658,000.\n\nLet me do 35,720 + 658,000:\n\n35,720 + 658,000. If I add 35,000 to 658,000, that's 693,000. Then add the remaining 720, so 693,000 +720= 693,720. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, so perhaps the user thought that the hundreds digit was 6 or something? Let me see 738 is 7 hundreds, 3 tens, 8 ones. So no, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the user multiplied 940 by 700 as 658,000, but then added something wrong. Let me see: if the user added 7,520 +28,200 = 35,720, then 35,720 +658,000 would indeed be 693,720. So unless the user made a mistake in one of the partial products.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made an error. Let me check the multiplication steps again.\n\nFirst step: 940 x8.\n\n940 x8:\n\n900x8=7200, 40x8=320. 7200+320=7520. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 940x30.\n\n30 is 3x10. So 940x3=2820, then times 10 gives 28,200. Correct.\n\nThird step:940x700.\n\n700 is 7x100. 940x7=6580, then x100 is 658,000. Correct.\n\nSo the answer should be 693,720. But the user wrote \"I think the correct answer is: 613720\". That's 613,720. There's a difference of 80,000. Hmm, so perhaps the user miscalculated the hundreds place.\n