200. Let\'s add 19,488 + 179,200:\n\n179,200 + 19,488:\n\n179,200 + 19,000 = 198,200.\n\nThen add 488 more: 198,200 + 488 = 198,688. So same result again.\n\nHmm, so the user\'s answer is 198,638, but my calculation gives 198,688. The difference is 50. Wait, where could I have gone wrong?\n\nWait, let me check the multiplication of 224 ×80 again. Wait, 224 ×80. Maybe I miscalculated that?\n\nWait 224 ×8 is 1,792. So times 10 is 17,920. That\'s correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the hundreds place? 224×800. 224×8 is 1,792. ×100 is 179,200. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the user\'s answer is wrong, but let me try another method. Let me compute 224 ×887 as (200 +24) × (800 +80 +7). But that might be complicated, but let\'s see.\n\nAlternatively, 224×887 = 224×(800 +80 +7) = 224×800 + 224×80 +224×7 = same as before, so same result. So 198,688.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use a calculator to verify. Wait, since I can\'t use a calculator, but let me do 224 × 800 = 179,200. 224×80=17,920. 224×7=1,568. Adding those:\n\n179,200 +17,920 = 197,120. Then +1,568 = 198,688. So that\'s correct.\n\nSo the user\'s answer of 198,638 is off by 50. Hmm. Maybe the user made a mistake in adding?\n\nWait let\'s see: 1568 +17920 +179200.\n\nWait, 1568 + 17920:\n\n1568 + 17,920.\n\n1568 + 17,920:\n\n17,920 + 1,500 = 19,420. Then add 68 more: 19,488. Then adding 179,200 gives 198,688. So that\'s correct. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem was written wrong? The user says the question is 224 and 887. Maybe the actual numbers are different? But according to the user\'s question, it\'s 224 ×887. So perhaps the user\'s answer is wrong. Alternatively, maybe I made a mistake in a step?\n\nWait let me check the multiplication of 224×8 again. 224×8: 200×8=1,600. 24×8=192. 1,600+192=1,792. That\'s correct. So 224×800 is indeed 179,200. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is 224 × 887, but the user thought 224 × 887 is 198,638, but actually it\'s 198,688. So the correct answer should be