on:\n\n\u202f\u202f 397\n\n\u00d7868\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply by 8 (units):\n\n397\u00d78 = 3,176\n\nThen multiply by 60 (tens place, so 6\u00d710):\n\n397\u00d76 =2,382, then add a zero \u2192 23,820\n\nThen multiply by 800 (hundreds place, 8\u00d7100):\n\n397\u00d78 =3,176, then add two zeros \u2192 317,600\n\nNow add all three:\n\n3,176\n\n23,820\n\n317,600\n\nAdding the first two: 3,176 +23,820 =26,996\n\n26,996 +317,600 =344,596\n\nYes, so I'm confident that the correct answer is 344,596. The user's answer is 343,596, which is 1,000 less. Perhaps they thought that 397\u00d7800 is 316,600? Let's see, 397\u00d7800: 397\u00d78\u00d7100. If someone miscalculates 397\u00d78 as 3,166 instead of 3,176, then 3,166\u00d7100=316,600. Then adding 26,996 gives 316,600+26,996 =343,596. So that's probably where the mistake is.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 344,596. I'll present the steps accordingly in the template.\n</think>\n\n",
