      "text": "625,800 + 16,986 = 642,786?\n\nWait, wait, let me check again. 625,800 plus 16,986.\n\nBreakdown:\n\n625,800 + 10,000 = 635,800.\n\n635,800 + 6,000 = 641,800.\n\n641,800 + 986 = 642,786.\n\nYes, so total is 642,786. \n\nWait, but the user initially thought the answer was 649,786. Hmm. That suggests maybe I made a mistake here.\n\nWait, let me check each step again carefully.\n\nFirst partial product: 894 *9.\n\n894 *9:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n800*9 = 7200,\n\n90*9 = 810,\n\n4*9 = 36.\n\nAdding those: 7200+810 = 8010; 8010+36=8046. That's correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 894 *10 (since the tens digit is 1, so 1*10). 894*10 is indeed 8940. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 894*700. Let's recalculate that.\n\n894 *700:\n\n894*7 = ?\n\nLet me compute 894*7 again:\n\n800*7 = 5600,\n\n90*7 = 630,\n\n4*7 =28.\n\n5600+630 is 6230, plus 28 is 6258. So 6258 *100 = 625,800. Correct.\n\nNow adding the three partial products:\n\nFirst: 8,046,\n\nSecond: 8,940,\n\nThird: 625,800.\n\nAdding first two: 8,046 +8,940.\n\nLet me do this again:\n\n8,046 +8,940.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6 +0=6,\n\n4 +4=8,\n\n0 (from 8,046's hundreds digit) +9 (from 8,940's hundreds digit)=9,\n\n8 (thousands place of first) +8 (thousands of second) =16. So total is 16,986. That's correct.\n\nAdding that to 625,800:\n\n625,800 +16,986.\n\nLet me add 625,800 +10,000 first =635,800.\n\nThen add the remaining 6,986:\n\n635,800 +6,000 =641,800,\n\n641,800 +986 =642,786.\n\nHmm, so the total is 642,786. But the user thought it was 649,786. There's a discrepancy here. Did I miscalculate?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the third partial product's place value? Let me check again.\n\nWait, when multiplying by the hundreds place, which is 7 in 719, so 700. So 894*700 is indeed 625,800. That's correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in adding?\n\nWait, let me try adding all three numbers together step by step:\n\nFirst, 8,046 (first partial product),\n\nplus 8,940 (second) = 16,986,\n\nplus