ding all three results together:.\n\nFirst, add 364 and 3640. Let's see, 364 + 3640. 364 + 3000 is 3364, plus 640 more? Wait, maybe better to align them:.\n\n  364.\n+3640.\n------.\n 4004?.\n\nWait, no. Let me add them properly. 364 plus 3640. Since 3640 is 3 thousands, 6 hundreds, 4 tens, 0 ones. Adding 364 (0 thousands, 3 hundreds, 6 tens, 4 ones). So:.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 0 = 3.\n\nHundreds place: 6 + 3 = 9.\n\nTens place: 4 + 6 = 10.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 4 = 4.\n\nWait, that would make it 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 10 (tens), 4 (ones). But 10 tens is 100, so actually that's 3 thousands + 9 hundreds + 10 tens +4 ones. Converting the 10 tens to 1 hundred, so adding 1 to the hundreds place:.\n\nSo total would be 3 thousands, 10 hundreds, 0 tens, 4 ones? Wait, that's getting confusing. Maybe better to write numerically:.\n\n3640.\n\n+\xa0 364.\n\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 0 +4 =4.\n\nTens place: 4 +6=10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 6 +3 +1 (carryover) =10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 3 +0 +1 (carryover) =4.\n\nSo total is 4004. Okay, so 364 + 3640 = 4004. Got it.\n\nNow add that to the third part, which is 72,800.\n\nSo 4004 + 72,800. Let's see:.\n\n72,800.\n\n+\xa0 4,004.\n\n= ?.\n\nAdding the thousands:.\n\n72,000 +4,000 =76,000.\n\nThen 800 +4=804. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
