e it's the tens place, it's 1\u00d710, so 750 \u00d710 = 7,500.\n\n3. Multiply 750 by the hundreds place digit (1), which is 1\u00d7100, so 750\u00d7100 = 75,000.\n\nAdding all three results: 0 + 7,500 +75,000 = 82,500. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 82,500. The user thought it was 82,900, which is incorrect. So I need to present the correct reasoning here. \n\nI should also check if there's an alternative way they might have gotten 82,900. Maybe miscalculating 750 \u00d711 as 8,250 but then adding an extra 400? Not sure, but regardless, the steps clearly add up to 82,500. \n\nAlright, proceeding with the correct answer and the step-by-step as per the template.\n</think>\n\n",
