ong? Or maybe I messed up the addition?\n\nWait let me do the addition again step by step:\n\nFirst part: 549\n\nSecond part: 12,810\n\nThird part:54,900\n\nAdding first two: 549 +12,810 = 13,359\n\nThen 13,359 +54,900: Let\'s add 13,359 +50,000 =63,359, then add 4,900 more: 63,359 +4,900 =68,259.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the user thought the hundreds digit was 3, but in the number 373, the hundreds digit is 3, so 300. That\'s correct. So maybe the user\'s answer is incorrect?\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the multiplication steps.\n\nAlternatively, let me try the multiplication the standard way:\n\n183 ×373.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n\u2003\u2003183\n\n×373\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 183 by 3 (units): 549.\n\nThen multiply 183 by 70 (tens place, so 7×10): 183×7=1281, then shift one position: 12810.\n\nThen multiply 183 by 300 (hundreds place, 3×100): 54900.\n\nAdding those together: 549 +12810 +54900 = 68,259. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the user intended a different problem? Wait the user\'s question was "What is the product of 183 and 373? I think the correct answer is: 58259".\n\nHmm, 58,259 vs my 68,259. The difference is exactly 10,000. That suggests that perhaps in one of the steps, there was an error in the hundreds place. Let me see.\n\nWait, when multiplying by 300, maybe the user thought 3×183 is 549, then ×100, so 54,900. That part is correct.\n\nBut perhaps in the tens place, they did 183 ×7×10 =12,810, but maybe they miscalculated 7×183?\n\nWait let me check 183×7 again:\n\n183 ×7:\n\n3×7=21, write down 1, carryover 2.\n\n8×7=56 plus 2 is 58. Write 8, carryover 5.\n\n1×7=7 plus 5 is 12. So 1281. Correct. So 12,810.\n\nHmm. So adding 549 +12,810 gives 13,359, then plus 54,900 gives 68,259. So unless there\'s a miscalculation here, the correct answer should be 68,259. The user\'s answer is 58,259, which is 10,000 less. Maybe they thought the hundreds digit was 2 instead of 3? Let me see. If the number was 273 instead