k step by step. <<number2 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n\n1. Multiply number1 977 by the ones place digit 0 of number2 940: 977 × 0 = 0.\n2. Multiply number1 977 by the tens place digit 40 of number2 940: 977 × 40 = 39,080.\n3. Multiply number1 977 by the hundreds place digit 900 of number2 940: 977 × 900 = 879,300.\nSum all the step results: 0 + 39,080 + 879,300 = 918,380.\nSo, the final computed product is 918,380.\n\nHence, the correct answer is 918380.\n\nI need to make sure the steps are clearly written in the reasoning section as per the template.\n\nYes, that should do it. The user\'s answer is wrong, so the correct answer is 918,380.\n'] 50%|#####     | 252/500 [6:43:53<8:00:59, 116.37s/it]
