×2 is 342, so times 100 is 34,200. Okay, that looks good.\n\nNow, I need to add up all those partial products: 171 + 11,970 + 34,200. Let's do this step by step. Adding the first two: 171 + 11,970. Let's see, 171 + 11,970. Adding the hundreds: 100 + 11,900 is 12,000, but wait, maybe better to line them up:.\n\n  171.\n+11970.\n= ?.\n\nAdding the units: 1 + 0 =1, tens:7 +7=14, so carry over 1. Then hundreds: 1 (from 171) +9 (from 11970) +1 carried over = 11. So that would be 12,141? Wait, hold on, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me recalculate.\n\nWait, maybe I should align the numbers properly:.\n\n171 is the same as 00171, and 11970 is 11970. So adding:.\n\n  00171.\n+11970.\n--------.\n  12141?.\n\nWait, 171 + 11,970. Let's see, 11,970 + 100 is 12,070, then plus 71 more is 12,141. Yeah, that's right.\n\nNow add the third number: 12,141 + 34,200. Let's add those. 12,000 + 34,200 is 46,200. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
