ce, the digit is 2 but represents 20. So 100 × 20. Third step is the hundreds place digit, which is 2, representing 200, so 100 × 200. Then add all three results together. .\n\nLet me compute each step. .\n\nFirst step: 100 × 6. Well, 100 times 6 is straightforward. 100×6 = 600. .\n\nSecond step: 100 × 20. Hmm, 100 multiplied by 20. Since 20 is 2×10, so 100×20 = 2000. .\n\nThird step: 100 × 200. That's 100×200. 200 is 2×100, so 100×200 = 20,000. .\n\nNow, adding all these up: 600 + 2000 + 20,000. Let me add the first two: 600 + 2000 = 2600. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
