ss terms?\n\nLet me try that approach:\n\n(900 +7)(300 +14) = 900×300 +900×14 +7×300 +7×14.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n900×300=270,000.\n\n900×14=12,600.\n\n7×300=2,100.\n\n7×14=98.\n\nNow add all together:\n\n270,000 +12,600 =282,600.\n\n282,600 +2,100 =284,700.\n\n284,700 +98 =284,798. Same result.\n\nHmm, so it\'s consistent. So I think the correct answer is indeed 284,798, and the user\'s thought of 284,795 is incorrect. Perhaps they made a mistake in one of the multiplication steps. Let me check again each step.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the first step? Let me recheck 907×4.\n\n900×4=3,600. 7×4=28. 3,600+28=3,628. Correct.\n\n907×10: 907×10 is 9,070. Correct.\n\n907×300: 907×3=2,721, so ×100 is 272,100. Correct.\n\nAdding 3,628 +9,070: 3,628 +9,070. Let\'s do it digit by digit:\n\n3,628\n\n+9,070\n\nUnits: 8+0=8.\n\nTens: 2+7=9.\n\nHundreds:6+0=6.\n\nThousands:3+9=12. So 12,698. Correct.\n\nAdding to 272,100:\n\n272,100 +12,698:\n\nBreakdown: 272,100 +10,000 =282,100.\n\n282,100 +2,698 =284,798. Correct.\n\nHmm. So unless there\'s a different interpretation of the question, but the numbers are 907 and 314. The user\'s answer is 284,795, which is 3 less than my result. Let me see: 284,798 minus 3 is 284,795. Where could that 3 come from?\n\nMaybe in the hundreds place calculation: if someone thought 3×907 is 2720 instead of 2721. Let me see:\n\n3×900=2700, 3×7=21. 2700+21=2721. So if someone miscalculates 3×7 as 20, then 2700+20=2720. Then 2720×100=272,000. Then adding 272,000 +12,698 would be 284,698. Still not 284,795. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe in the tens place calculation: 1×907=907, but if they thought it\'s 10×907=9070, which is correct, but maybe they added it wrong? Like 9070 +3628. Let me see: 9070 +3628.\n\n9000+3000=12000.\n\n70+628=698.\n\nTotal 12,698. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps they thought that the hundreds digit is 30 instead of 300? Wait, 314\'s hundreds digit is 3, so 3×100=300. So that\'s correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they