ubtract 4×600 =2,400 and add back 4×1? Wait no, that might complicate. Alternatively, 196×599:\n\nBreak down 599 into 500 +90 +9. Then:\n\n196×500 =98,000\n\n196×90=17,640\n\n196×9=1,764\n\nAdding them all: 98,000 +17,640 =115,640; then +1,764 gives 117,404. Yes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 117,404, not 217,404. The user might have made an error in their calculation, perhaps miscalculating the hundreds place as 600 instead of 500? 196×600 would be 117,600, and if they added that to the other parts incorrectly, but not sure.\n\nIn any case, following the reasoning steps as per the template, the correct answer is 117,404. So I should present that in the required format.\n'] 63%|######2   | 314/500 [8:11:42<5:05:43, 98.62s/it] 
