Correct.\n\nNow I need to add all three results together: 2052 (from the ones), 9120 (from the tens), and 91,200 (from the hundreds). Let me line them up properly:.\n\n   2052.\n+  9120.\n+91200.\n--------.\n?.\n\nAdding the first two: 2052 + 9120. Let's see, 2000 + 9000 = 11,000. 52 + 120 = 172. So total is 11,000 + 172 = 11,172. Wait, actually, that might not be the right way. Let me do it step by step:.\n\n2052 + 9120:.\n2000 + 9000 = 11,000.\n50 + 120 = 170.\n2 + 0 = 2.\nWait, maybe it's easier to add digit by digit:.\n\n2052.\n+9120.\n= (2000 + 9000) + (50 + 120) + (2 + 0) = 11000 + 170 + 2 = 11,172. Okay, that's correct.\n\nNow add that to 91,200:.\n\n11,172 + 91,200. Let's see, 11,000 + 91,000 = 102,000. Then 172 + 200 = 372. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
