confirm again. Alternatively, maybe I should do it step by step again. .\n\nWait, 799 × 80: 80 is 8×10, so 799×8×10. 799×8: 700×8=5600, 90×8=720, 9×8=72. Adding those: 5600+720 is 6320, plus 72 is 6392. Then times 10 is 63,920. Yeah, that's correct.\n\nNow the hundreds place of 685 is 6, which is actually 600. So multiply 799 by 600. Again, breaking it down: 799 × 6 × 100. .\n\n799 ×6: 700×6=4200, 90×6=540, 9×6=54. Adding those: 4200+540 is 4740, plus 54 is 4794. Then multiply by 100 to get 479,400.\n\nNow I have the three parts: 3,995 (from the ones place), 63,920 (from the tens place), and 479,400 (from the hundreds place). .\n\nAdding them all together: Let's start with the first two. 3,995 + 63,920. 3,995 + 60,000 is 63,995, then +3,920? Wait no, wait, 63,920 is 63 thousand plus 920. Wait, actually, 3,995 + 63,920. Let's do it digit by digit:.\n\n3,995  .\n+63,920  .\n= ?.\n\nAdding the ones place: 5+0=5  .\nTens: 9+2=11, write 1 carryover 1  .\nHundreds: 9 +9 +1=19, write 9 carryover 1  .\nThousands: 3 +3 +1=7  .\nTen-thousands: 6  .\nWait, maybe better to align them properly:.\n\n  3995  .\n+63920  .\n--------.\nStarting from the right:.\nOnes: 5 +0=5  .\nTens:9 +2=11, so write 1 carryover 1  .\nHundreds:9 +9=18 plus the 1 is 19, write 9 carryover1  .\nThousands:3 +3=6 plus the 1 is 7  .\nTen-thousands:6  .\nSo total is 67,915? Wait, wait, 3995 +63920:.\n\nWait 3,995 +63,920. Let me do 63,920 + 3,000 is 66,920, then add 995 more: 66,920 + 995 = 67,915. Yes, that's correct. .\n\nNow add the last part, which is 479,400. .\n\nSo 67,915 + 479,400. Let's compute that. .\n\nAdding 67,915 + 400,000 = 467,915  .\nThen add 79,400 more? Wait, no. Wait 479,400 is 400,000 +79,400. .\n\nAlternatively, 479,400 + 67,915: .\n\n479,400  .\n+ 67,915  .\n= ?.\n\nAdding:.\n\nOnes:0 +5=5  .\nTens:0 +1=1  .\nHundreds:4 +9=13, carryover 1  .\nThousands:9 +7=16 plus 1 is 17, carryover1  .\nTen-thousands:7 +6=13 plus 1 is14, carryover1  .\nHundred thousands:4 +0=4 plus 1 is 5. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
