s:6\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:3\n\nUnits:2\n\nWait, but that would be 256,932. Which matches my previous result. So the total is 256,932. But the user thought it was 256,832. Hmm. So maybe their answer was wrong? Or did I make an error?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in one of the multiplications. Let me check each multiplication again.\n\nFirst step: 793 ×4:\n\n700×4=2800\n\n90×4=360\n\n3×4=12\n\nTotal:2800+360=3160 +12=3172. That's correct.\n\nSecond step:793×20. 793×2=1586. ×10 gives 15,860. Correct.\n\nThird step:793×300. 793×3=2379, ×100 gives 237,900. Correct.\n\nAdding 3172 +15,860 =19,032. Then 19,032 +237,900.\n\nWait, 237,900 +19,032:\n\n237,900 +10,000 =247,900\n\n247,900 +9,032 =256,932. Yes, so that's correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the user's answer was incorrect. Alternatively, perhaps I miscalculated somewhere else. Let me try multiplying 793 ×324 in another way to verify.\n\nAnother way: 793 ×324 =793 ×(300+24) =793×300 +793×24.\n\nCompute 793×300 =237,900 as before.\n\nNow 793×24:\n\nBreakdown: 793×20 +793×4.\n\n793×20=15,860\n\n793×4=3,172 (same as before)\n\nAdding those gives 15,860 +3,172 =19,032. Then total is 237,900 +19,032=256,932. So same result.\n\nAlternatively, using standard multiplication:\n\nMultiply 793 ×324:\n\nFirst, write 793\n\n×\xa0324\n\n------------\n\nMultiply by 4: 793×4=3,172\n\nMultiply by 20: 793×20=15,860\n\nMultiply by 300:793×300=237,900\n\nAdd them all:3,172 +15,860 +237,900 =256,932.\n\nYes, so that's correct. The user's answer of 256,832 must be wrong, probably due to an arithmetic mistake in their calculation. Let me see where they might have gone wrong. Maybe in adding the numbers?\n\nSuppose they did 3,172 +15,860 =19,032. Then adding to 237,900:\n\nIf they thought 237,900 +19,032 as 237,900 +19,000 =256,900, then plus 32 is 256,932. So that's correct. Alternatively, maybe they miscalculated 793×20 as 15,860? Let me see, 793×20 is indeed 15,860. Alternatively, maybe they thought 793×300 as 237,000, missing the 90