      "text": "673,326? Wait, but the user thought the answer was 673,322. Hmm, so maybe I made an error in calculation somewhere.\n\nWait, let me recheck each step again.\n\nFirst step: 674 \u00d79 = 6,066. That's correct because 600\u00d79=5,400; 70\u00d79=630 (total so far 5,400+630=6,030); 4\u00d79=36. 6,030+36=6,066. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 674\u00d790. Since 90 is 9\u00d710, so 6,066\u00d710=60,660. Correct.\n\nThird step: 674\u00d7900. 900 is 9\u00d7100, so 6,066\u00d7100=606,600. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 6,066 + 60,660 = 66,726. Then 66,726 +606,600. Let me do this addition again carefully:\n\n66,726\n\n+606,600\n\nFirst, adding 66,726 and 606,600:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n66,726\n\n606,600\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from units:\n\n6+0=6\n\n2+0=2\n\n7+6=13 (carryover 1)\n\n6 (thousands place of first number) +6 (thousands place of second number) +1 (carryover) = 13. So write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 6 (from first number's ten thousands place) +0 (second number's ten thousands place is 0) +1 (carryover) =7\n\nHundred thousands place: 0 (from first number) +6 (second number) =6.\n\nSo total is 673,326.\n\nHmm, so that's different from the user's answer of 673,322. Where did they go wrong?\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the multiplication steps.\n\nWait, let me try an alternative method to verify. Let's compute 674 \u00d7 999.\n\nAnother way: 999 is 1000 -1. So, 674\u00d7(1000-1)=674\u00d71000 -674\u00d71=674,000 -674=673,326. Exactly the same result as before. So that confirms that the correct answer is 673,326. The user thought it was 673,322, which is off by 4. Probably an arithmetic error in their steps. \n\nWait, maybe I miscalculated when adding 66,726 and 606,600. Let me check again:\n\n66,726 + 606,600.\n\nLet me add 66,726 + 600,000 first: that gives 666,726. Then add the remaining 6,600. Wait, no, 606,600 is 600,000 +6,600. Wait, 606,600 is 600k plus 6,600? Wait no: 600,000 +6,600 =606,600. So 66,726 +606,600 = (66,726 +6