22. Then adding 606,600 gives 66,722 +606,600=673,322. Ah! So that's the mistake. So if they miscalculated 674\u00d79 as 6,062 instead of 6,066, then the total would be 673,322. Let's verify:\n\n674\u00d79:\n\nBreakdown: 600\u00d79=5,400; 70\u00d79=630; 4\u00d79=36. \n\n5,400 +630 =6,030. Then +36 is 6,066. If they did 5,400 +630 =6,030, but then added 30 instead of 36, getting 6,060, then +6=6,066. Wait, but how would they get 6,062? Maybe they thought 4\u00d79=32? No, that's 36. Alternatively, 600\u00d79=5,400; 70\u00d79=630 (total 6,030); then 4\u00d79=36, but added 6,030 +36 =6,066. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they added 600\u00d79=5,400; then 70\u00d79=630 \u2192 total 5,400+630=6,030. Then 4\u00d79=36. 6,030 +36=6,066. Correct. \n\nHmm, unless they miscalculated 70\u00d79 as 620 instead of 630, leading to 5,400+620=6,020. Then +36=6,056. Not matching. Alternatively, if they messed up the 70\u00d79 as 63\u00d710=630. Wait, maybe they did 7\u00d79=63, so 70\u00d79=630. Correct. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps they did 674\u00d79 as (600+74)\u00d79 =5,400 + 666 (since 74\u00d79=666). 5,400 +666=6,066. So that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 674\u00d79 as 674\u00d710 minus 674, which is 6,740 -674=6,066. Correct. \n\nHmm, so the only way to get 6,062 is if they made an error in that first multiplication step, like miscalculating 600\u00d79 as 5,400 (correct), but then 70\u00d79 as 620 (wrong) instead of 630, then 4\u00d79=36. So 5,400 +620=6,020 +36=6,056, still not 6,062. Alternatively, 674\u00d79= (670 +4)\u00d79 =6,030 +36=6,066. So unless there's a different error. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 674\u00d79 as 600\u00d79=5,400; 70\u00d79=630; 4\u00d79=36. Then added 5,400+630=6,030, then added 36 to get 6,066. But if they added 5,400+630=6,030, then added 32 instead of 36, getting 6,062. That could be a simple addition error in the last step. So 6,030 +32=6,062. Then the rest of the steps would lead to 673,322. So that's probably where the mistake occur