ent error. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 674×9 as 600×9=5,400; 70×9=630; 4×9=36. Then added 5,400+630=6,030, then added 36 to get 6,066. But if they added 5,400+630=6,030, then added 32 instead of 36, getting 6,062. That could be a simple addition error in the last step. So 6,030 +32=6,062. Then the rest of the steps would lead to 673,322. So that's probably where the mistake occurred.\n\nIn any case, the correct product is 673,326. So I'll present that as the answer with the step-by-step reasoning as per the template.\n\n"] 76%|#######6  | 380/500 [9:55:30<3:49:57, 114.98s/it]
