ill not matching.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 206\u00d7428 as follows: 200\u00d7428 +6\u00d7428.\n\n200\u00d7428 is 85,600.\n\n6\u00d7428: 6\u00d7400=2400, 6\u00d728=168, so total 2400+168=2568.\n\nAdding 85,600 +2,568: 85,600 +2,000=87,600 +568=88,168. Correct again.\n\nHmm, so I can't see where they got 88,128. Maybe a typo? Or miscalculating 206\u00d7428 as 206\u00d7420 +206\u00d78. Let's see:\n\n206\u00d7420: 206\u00d7400=82,400; 206\u00d720=4,120. Total 82,400+4,120=86,520. Then add 206\u00d78=1,648. Total 86,520 +1,648 = 88,168. Still same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they thought 206\u00d7428 is (200+6)(400+28)= 200\u00d7400 +200\u00d728 +6\u00d7400 +6\u00d728. Let me compute each term:\n\n200\u00d7400=80,000\n\n200\u00d728=5,600 (since 200\u00d720=4,000 and 200\u00d78=1,600, total 5,600)\n\n6\u00d7400=2,400\n\n6\u00d728=168\n\nAdding all: 80,000 +5,600=85,600 +2,400=88,000 +168=88,168. Same again.\n\nHmm. I can't find a way to get 88,128 unless there's an error in one of the steps. Wait, maybe they did 206\u00d7428 as 200\u00d7400 + 200\u00d728 +6\u00d7400 +6\u00d720\u00d7 something. Wait, maybe a miscalculation in the 200\u00d728? Let me see: 200\u00d728 is 5,600. If someone miscalculates that as 5,200, then total would be 80,000+5,200=85,200 +2,400=87,600 +168=87,768. Not matching.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 206\u00d7428 as 206\u00d7(400+20+8)=206\u00d7400 +206\u00d720 +206\u00d78, but miscalculated 206\u00d720 as 4000 (which is wrong because 206\u00d720 is 4,120). If they did 4000 instead, then 82,400+4,000=86,400 +1,648=88,048. Not the answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they added the numbers wrong. Let me see:\n\nIf they had 1648 + 4120 +82,400:\n\nSuppose they added 1648 +4120 first, but got 5768. Then added 82,400 +5,768. Wait, 82,400 +5,000 is 87,400, plus 768 is 88,168. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they thought 82,400 +4,120 +1,648? Wait, no, that would be same as before.\n\nHmm, maybe the user made a typo and the correct answer is indeed 88