ut that would be 772\u00d7(380-1) = 772\u00d7380 -772. Let's see:\n\n772\u00d7380: 772\u00d738 \u00d710. 772\u00d738. Let's compute that. 772\u00d730=23,160 and 772\u00d78=6,176. Summing 23,160 +6,176=29,336. Then \u00d710 gives 293,360. Then subtract 772: 293,360 -772 = 292,588. Same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 292,588. But the user says they think it's 792,588. That's different. Maybe they made a mistake in their calculation? Let me see why they thought 792,588.\n\nWait, 792,588 is 700,000+90,000+..., but perhaps they added an extra digit somewhere. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 772 \u00d7379 as follows:\n\nWait, maybe they did 772 \u00d7300 =231,600,\n\n772 \u00d770 =54,040,\n\n772 \u00d79 =6,948,\n\nBut then adding 231,600 +54,040 =285,640 +6,948 =292,588. Same as before. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps they did 772 \u00d7379 as:\n\nFirst, 700\u00d7300=210,000,\n\n700\u00d770=49,000,\n\n700\u00d79=6,300,\n\nThen 70\u00d7300=21,000,\n\n70\u00d770=4,900,\n\n70\u00d79=630,\n\nThen 2\u00d7300=600,\n\n2\u00d770=140,\n\n2\u00d79=18,\n\nBut that's breaking down both numbers into hundreds, tens, ones. That might be too complicated, but let's see:\n\nWait, breaking 772 into 700 +70 +2,\n\nand 379 into 300 +70 +9,\n\nthen multiply each term:\n\n(700)(300) = 210,000,\n\n(700)(70)=49,000,\n\n(700)(9)=6,300,\n\n(70)(300)=21,000,\n\n(70)(70)=4,900,\n\n(70)(9)=630,\n\n(2)(300)=600,\n\n(2)(70)=140,\n\n(2)(9)=18.\n\nNow adding all these together:\n\n210,000 +49,000 =259,000,\n\n259,000 +6,300 =265,300,\n\n265,300 +21,000 =286,300,\n\n286,300 +4,900 =291,200,\n\n291,200 +630 =291,830,\n\n291,830 +600 =292,430,\n\n292,430 +140 =292,570,\n\n292,570 +18 =292,588.\n\nSame result again. So the correct answer is 292,588. Therefore, the user's thought that it's 792,588 must be incorrect. Maybe they added an extra 500,000 somewhere? Like maybe miscalculating 772\u00d7300 as 2,316,000 instead of 231,600? If that were the case, then a