r2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n\nSo the structure is that the reasoning lists the steps, then the answer section has a line starting with "Now, sum...", then the final answer.\n\nTherefore, following that structure:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 772 and 379?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet\'s think step by step. 379 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 772 by the ones place digit 9 of 379:  \n   772 × 9 = 6,948.\n\n2. Multiply 772 by the tens place digit 70 (since 7 is in the tens place) of 379:  \n   772 × 70 = 54,040.\n\n3. Multiply 772 by the hundreds place digit 300 (since 3 is in the hundreds place) of 379:  \n   772 × 300 = 231,600.\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: 6,948 + 54,040 + 231,600 = 292,588.  \nSo, the final computed product is 292,588.\n\nI think that\'s the correct way to fill it in. The user\'s initial thought was 792,588, but the correct answer is 292,588. So the answer section should reflect the correct one.\n'] 94%|#########3| 468/500 [12:08:46<50:30, 94.71s/it]
