y 921 as follows:\n\nFirst, 491 × 900 = 441,900.\n\nThen, 491 × 21 = 491 ×20 + 491×1 =9,820 +491 =10,311.\n\nAdding 441,900 +10,311 gives 452,211. So that\'s correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the user intended a different problem? Let me check if the numbers were swapped, but the question states 491 and 921. Alternatively, perhaps they thought 491 × 921 is 491 ×920 + 491×1, but even that would be 491×920. Let\'s see:\n\n491 ×920: 491×900=441,900 and 491×20=9,820. So total is same as before, plus the 1×491 gives the same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they did 491×921 as (400+90+1)×(900+20+1), expanding all terms, but that would be tedious but should also give the same.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps they miscalculated 491 ×900 as 441,000 instead of 441,900. Let\'s see:\n\n441,000 +10,311 =451,311 +491=451,802? Wait, no. Wait, if they thought 491×900=441,000, then adding 10,311 (from 9,820+491) would be 441,000 +10,311=451,311. Which is still not 456,211.\n\nAlternatively, maybe they multiplied 491×921 as (491×9)×100 + (491×21). Let me see:\n\n491×9=4,419. Then ×100 is 441,900. 491×21=10,311. So total is same as before. \n\nHmm, I can\'t figure out how they got 456,211. Maybe they added an extra 4,000 somewhere. Let me see:\n\nIf they thought the partial product for 491×900 was 445,900 instead of 441,900, then adding 10,311 would give 456,211. That would be the case if they multiplied 491×9 as 4,459 instead of 4,419. Let\'s check 491×9:\n\n400×9=3,600; 90×9=810; 1×9=9. 3,600+810=4,410; +9=4,419. So if someone added wrong, like 3,600+800=4,400 instead of 810, then 4,400 +9=4,409, but that\'s not 4,459. Alternatively, miscalculating 491×9 as 4,459 (maybe 400×9=3,600 plus 90×9=810, but they added 3,600+810 as 4,410, then 1×9=9, totaling 4,419. So unless they added 400×9=3,600, 90×9=810, but then 3,600 +810 is 4,410, then 4,410+9=4,419. So unless someone thought 491×9 is 4,459, that would lead to 445,900. Then adding 10,311 would give 456,211. So perhaps they made that mistake in the multiplication step. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 452,211, and the user\'s thought of 456,211 is incorrect due to an error in calculating 491 ×900 as 445,900 instead of 441,900. \n\nAlright, so I need to present the correct solution following the template. Let me structure it step by step as per the example given.\n\nThe user\'s question is to find the product of 491 and 921. The correct answer is 452,211, so I\'ll explain the steps accordingly.\n'] 95%|#########5| 476/500 [12:22:39<43:01, 107.54s/it]
